  "interpretation_boundary": "Measurements compare independent host-PDC-compensated Ableton exports of the installed legacy Maag EQ4 VST3 family over one deterministic 72-second fixture. They establish the active all-gains-zero boundary, the broad steady-state transfer of the 20 kHz Air Band at a non-clipping +3 dB state, the headroom failure observed at +5 dB on this fixture, stereo consistency, peak/level consequences, and the host-reported zero-latency state at 48 kHz. Triangular dither prevents a bit-perfect null. Simultaneous tones provide reliable comparative transfer at the listed bins for this linear fixed-EQ case but do not replace swept-sine distortion testing. The experiment does not establish every fixed band, Level Trim behavior, automation, noise or harmonic distortion below the fixture/dither floor, CPU cost, other sample rates/formats, newer Maag EQ4 builds, or musical preference."
}
